, NJ"],["High School","North 13th Street"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2026/9/25/Harris_Purcell.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/harrison-purcell/11794","d":1795216876788},"Jordan Pishko":{"f":[["Ciudad","Rockledge, Florida"],["Instituto","Keiser University"],["Curso","Junior"],["Position","First Base/Catcher"],["Height","6-1"],["Weight","210"],["Class","Freshman"],["Hometown","Newark, NJ"],["High School","North 13th Street"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2026/9/25/Jordan_Pishko.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/jordan-pishko/11805","d":1795216876839},"Carter Redelman":{"f":[["Ciudad","Morgantown, W. Va."],["Instituto","Morgantown HS/Fairmont State"],["Universidad anterior","Fairmont State"],["Curso","Senior"],["Position","First Base/Catcher"],["Height","6-1"],["Weight","210"],["Class","Freshman"],["Hometown","Newark, NJ"],["High School","North 13th Street"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2026/9/25/Carter_Redelman.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/carter-redelman/11775","d":1795216876882},"Arthur Neighbors":{"f":[["Ciudad","Greensboro, N.C."],["Instituto","Cornerstone Charter Academy"],["Curso","Freshman"],["Position","First Base/Catcher"],["Height","6-1"],["Weight","210"],["Class","Freshman"],["Hometown","Newark, NJ"],["High School","North 13th Street"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2026/9/25/Arthur_Neighbors.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/arthur-neighbors/11792","d":1795216876969},"Jake Thomas":{"f":[["Ciudad","Knoxville, Tenn."],["Instituto","Knoxville Central HS"],["Curso","Freshman"],["Position","First Base/Catcher"],["Height","6-1"],["Weight","210"],["Class","Freshman"],["Hometown","Newark, NJ"],["High School","North 13th Street"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2026/9/25/Jake_Thomas.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/jake-thomas/11795","d":1795216877520},"Luke Weber":{"f":[["Ciudad","Charlotte, N.C."],["Instituto","Community School of Davidson"],["Curso","Senior"],["Position","First Base/Catcher"],["Height","6-1"],["Weight","210"],["Class","Freshman"],["Hometown","Newark, NJ"],["High School","North 13th Street"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2026/9/25/Luke_Weber.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/luke-weber/11781","d":1795216877599},"Aaron Willis":{"f":[["Ciudad","Columbia, S.C."],["Instituto","Gray Collegiate"],["Curso","Freshman"],["Position","First Base/Catcher"],["Height","6-1"],["Weight","210"],["Class","Freshman"],["Hometown","Newark, NJ"],["High School","North 13th Street"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2026/9/25/Aaron_Willis.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/aaron-willis/11796","d":1795216877903}},"c":{"Ashley Kaminski":{"f":[["Cargo","Assistant Coach"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2024/10/3/6H4A2499.JPG","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/coaches/ashley-kaminski/1325","d":1795216709088},"Mike Blum":{"b":"Mike Blum is entering his third season as the head coach for the Gardner-Webb men's and women's swimming programs.\nIn Blum's second season at the helm of the program, he led the men's team to their first CCSA Conference championship in school history. The Men and Women had a combined total of 24 CCSA All-Conference Finishes at the championship meet (22 Individual and 4 Relays). Blum was also awarded CCSA Co-Coach of the Year by the conference office at the conclusion of the CCSA Conference Championship.\nDuring Blum’s first season as head coach for Gardner-Webb, he took the men’s team to second place and the women’s team to seventh overall at the CCSA Championships.\nBlum, who was an assistant at Gardner-Webb for the 2011-12 season, returned to Gardner-Webb for the 2019-20 season after most recently spending time on the staff at the University of North Carolina, where he helped guide seven swimmers to qualify for the 2019 NCAA Division I Championships.\nPrior to joining the staff at North Carolina, Blum was the head coach at Florida Southern College in Lakeland, Fla. for three seasons. His teams totaled 45 NCAA Division II qualifiers, and had 88 NCAA D-II All-American award winners. He had two relay teams win NCAA championships, as well as one individual championship and was named the 2016 CSCAA Men's Swimming National Coach of the Year.\n\"I would like to thank Vice President for Athletics Chuck Burch and the Gardner-Webb University administration for this amazing opportunity,\" Blum said. \"This is a special team and I feel honored to have been chosen to be a part of it. My family and I are excited to get back to Boiling Springs and we are excited to raise our son in such an amazing community. We are looking forward to the to the upcoming season and many more after.\"\nBlum was an assistant at Florida Southern for two different three-year stints, where his swimmers won seven NCAA D-II national championships and earned 56 All-American honors. He also saw two swimmers qualify for the 2013 World Championships and one qualifier for the 2012 Summer Olympic Games in London.\nBlum was an assistant for the 2011-12 season at Gardner-Webb, in which his swimmers set six new school records. That season, the men's team placed third at the 2012 Coastal Collegiate Sports Association (CCSA) Championships, while the women's squad took home a fourth-place result.\n\"Mike has great experience, shares an understanding of the overall mission here at Gardner-Webb University and will be a tremendous leader for our swim programs going forward,\" Vice President for Athletics Chuck Burch said. \"His vision for the programs and commitment to the overall development of our student-athletes are parallel to our expectations. We are excited to have him on campus soon.\"\nSince March 2012, Blum has also been the head coach and owner of the Lakeland Area Swimming club program, guiding numerous Florida Age Group qualifiers and champions, and instructed swimmers that took part in the 2012 and 2016 Summer Olympics in the 400-meter freestyle and the 100-meter butterfly.\nHe also spent time as an assistant senior coach at the Venice YMCA in Sarasota, Fla from August 2010 to March 2011, where he coached four FHSAA state qualifiers, one FHSAA state champion, one Senior National and Olympic Trials qualifier and the 2011 Florida Swimming Senior Championship team champions.\nBlum, who is originally from New Port Richey, Fla., is a 2008 graduate of Florida Southern College, where he received a Bachelor of Arts degree in Physical Education.","f":[["Cargo","Head Coach"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2020/1/15/MikeBlum_Ayhoz.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/coaches/mike-blum/1323","d":1795216709494},"Michael Southward":{"b":"In 2023-2024, Southward enters his first season as an assistant coach with the Runnin' Bulldogs after spending the 2022-2023 season as head coach at Saint Leo University.\nSouthward took over St. Leo's program in May of 2022 after completing the previous season as interim head coach. During Southward's tutelage, nine St. Leo swimmers earned All-America honors at the 2022 NCAA Division II National Championships.\nIn total, Southward spent two seasons at his alma mater, starting as a graduate assistant coach in the fall of 2021.\nPrior to his coaching career, Southward swam at Saint Leo from 2016-2020, serving as a team captain in both his junior and senior seasons. He was a member of the school record-holding 400-freestyle relay team which posted a mark of 2:57.06 at the 2018 national championships. Southward earned All-America honors at that meet and was also part of the 200-freestyle relay team that finished 11th nationally.\nAdditionally, Southward spent his summers as a coach in Pennsylvania developing youth swimmers at the Woodridge Swim Club in 2018 and 2019.\nSouthward graduated from Saint Leo in May of 2020 with a Bachelor of Arts in marketing.","f":[["Cargo","Assistant Coach"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2023/8/7/Michael_Southward_HS_OOmfJ.png","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/coaches/michael-southward/1324","d":1795216709510},"Gavin Gerwick":{"f":[["Cargo","Graduate Assistant Coach"]],"img":"https://gwusports.com/images/2026/9/25/Gavin_Gerwick.jpg","u":"https://gwusports.com/sports/swim/roster/coaches/gavin-gerwick/1326","d":1795216709638}}}